  "result": "This looks correct. All the fixes are in place:\n\n1. **Labels**: `assertOwnLabels` validates every `labelId` belongs to the org before attaching (createIssue + updateIssue).\n2. **Parent issue**: `assertLiveParentInProject` requires a live issue in the same project (rejects cross-workspace, cross-project, and archived parents as not-found).\n3. **Replies**: `createComment` now requires the parent comment to be live, top-level, and on the same issue.\n4. **Assignee/lead membership**: `assignIssue`, `createIssue`, `createProject`, and `updateProject` now require the target user to be a current member via `memberRepo.findMember`.\n5. **Mentions**: client-supplied `mentionedUserIds` are now filtered to current org members, not merged in unchecked.\n\nAll refusals throw `NotFoundError` (mapped to `not_found`), so a rejected write throws before any repository mutation happens — matching \"a refused change changes nothing.\" Typecheck is clean and the full test suite (617 tests) passes.",
